My take on this is that it’s not even really Mistral's fault. They actually have lots of clients and more than a decent amount of GPUs and datacenters compared to other open actors.

But there is very little (none?) competition in Europe on the 'frontier' LLM aspect, so they just have to build a 'good enough' model. Clients choose them because they are European and/or open weight, and the fact that enterprises can deploy Mistral models on their own infrastructure is a big deal for some companies. So they don’t have to compete on model capabilities with OpenAI and Anthropic.

