Very nice release by Mistral, with a technical report. They replace the complicated scaffold of previous lean models with a simple coding agent and scale test time compute budget with compaction every 200k steps.

It's also interesting that the impact of compaction isn't clearly visible in the training curve, possibly explaining diminishing returns. The training involved around 6 billion tokens, with supervised fine-tuning on 50% lean traces and reinforcement learning with CISPO.

